**2 [[Tackey]]s spawn after 66.67 seconds<sup>2,000f</sup>, delay 73.33~76.67 seconds<sup>2,200f~2,300f</sup>.
**5 [[Sir Rel]]s spawn after 146.67 seconds<sup>4,400f</sup>, delay 4~6 seconds<sup>120f~180f</sup>.
**6 [[Sir Rel]]s spawn after 233.33 seconds<sup>7,000f</sup>, delay 3.33~5.33 seconds<sup>100f~160f</sup>.

==Strategy==
The main problems of this stage are the over-buffed Tackeys, Golem Sunfish, and Papaou, two backliners that push the latter forward. Tackey can be eliminated with the help of LD units (Ubers are highly recommended), and the Sunfish won't be much of an issue until the cleanup phase. The periodic waves of Sir Rels, Ragin' Gories, and Doge Darks can be dealt with fairly easily if you defend Urs well.

==='''Recommended Units'''===
*[[Ancient Egg: N111 (Super Rare Cat)|Cop Cat]] - With Behemoth Slayer and [[Strong|Strong VS]] Traitless, he can deal insanely high damage to Papaou. Even with the Golem Sunfish's occasional curse ability, he retains his Behemoth Slayer properties, making him especially useful for the Ragin' Gories too. An absolute must-pick for this stage, especially since cash isn't too much of a concern.
*[[Weightlifter Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Pizza Cat]] - At higher levels, Pizza Cat shuts down every Black peon in this stage for the entire of its duration. His [[Wave Attack]] Talent synergizes very well with the nonstop enemy flow of this stage, as he can continuously deal damage to the Tackeys while chipping at the Sir Rels in the process.
*[[Ancient Egg: N101 (Rare Cat)|Courier Cat]] - Self-explanatory, but his Behemoth Slayer can chip at half of the enemies in this stage for absurd damage. And for such a cheap cost, Courier is a no-brainer.
*[[Stone Cat (Rare Cat)|Stone Cat]] - Given the high DPS of the Ragin' Gories and Sir Rels, Stone is very good at holding the frontline where other meatshields may fail. Works best with Research [[Cat Combo]]s.
*[[Dogumaru (Special Cat)|Reborn Warrior Doguemon]] - With his Curse immunity, [[Resistant]] to both Traitless and Relic, and Behemoth Slayer, he can stall out every enemy in this stage nigh-indefinitely. The one exception is Doge Dark, who chews through his HP faster than Sir Rel. Be careful to defend him, and he will serve as an excellent wall for the foreseeable future.

==='''Recommended Ubers'''===
*[[Izanami of Dusk (Legend Rare Cat)|Izanami of Eventide]] - Surprisingly, an excellent pick for this stage. Her [[Insane Damage]] against Traitless enemies proves to be a detriment for the boss of this stage, and it doesn't take her very long to reduce Papaou to a carcass in her short lifespan. She doesn't fare well against most other enemies in this stage, so time her [[Conjure]] ability and defend her well to allow her the most opportunities to [[Savage Blow]].
*[[Greater Balrog Cat]] - Low cost, low cooldown, very high single-target damage. Works wonders against Elephantidae, even without talents. He can survive 4 hits from Papaou at each of his knockbacks at level 55, which allows him to land a single blow before getting knocked back. If you do use him, make sure the path is clear, as if Balrog gets stuck on peons, he can be considered a waste.
*[[Kasa Jizo (Uber Rare Cat)|Kasa Jizo]] - Can be used as a substitute for Pizza Cat in Normal Form. His higher speed comes in especially handy for minimizing Golem Sunfish's damage against him; since some of Pizza Cat's main problems are his price, speed, and recharge, Kasa Jizo is an excellent substitute for a more spammable anti-Dark specialist. However, his damage is less than Pizza Cat's, so beware. If you happen to have his Ultra Form, he becomes even better, especially if you have his Curse Immunity Talent.
*[[King of Doom Phono (Uber Rare Cat)|King of Extinction Phono]] - Although Papaou is immune to [[Slow]] and [[Mini-Surge]], every other enemy in this stage isn't. It turns out Tackeys, Sir Rels, Doge Darks, and Ragin' Gories would typically prefer moving a lot of the time. If they can't move, then they can't push, which is especially true for enemies with fast attack rates and even faster movement speeds, such as them. It should be noted that he will die eventually due to Golem Sunfish's ludicrous damage, and if Tackey lands a lucky shot.

